# AGENTS.md

Module-specific guidance for the scaffolded API. Follow your repository
root `AGENTS.md` first.

## Module role

This is a Go HTTP API module scaffolded from the ERun `erun-backend-api`
blueprint via the `erun-scaffold-api` skill. It expects an
`erun-backend-db`-shaped PostgreSQL database with the `erun_tenant` /
`erun_operations` roles and the `erun_current_tenant_id()` function.

## Layer layout

- `internal/model/` — Bun-tagged structs mapping to database tables.
- `internal/repository/` — SQL via Bun. CRUD only (`Create`/`Get`/`List`/`Update`).
- `internal/service/` — workflows. **Create files here only when a workflow has real logic beyond calling one repository method.**
- `internal/routes/` — HTTP adaptation; one file per entity.
- `server.go` — composition boundary; constructs repos, optional services, routes, middleware.

Import direction: `routes` → (`services` or `repositories`) → `model`.
`model` must not import from API layers.

## Authentication and authorization

- OIDC bearer required on every protected route.
- Token issuer maps to tenant; `(issuer, subject)` maps to ERun user.
- Empty database: first authenticated identity bootstraps OPERATIONS
  tenant + first user with `ReadAll` + `WriteAll`. Once any tenant
  exists, unknown identities are 401.
- Authorization middleware matches the canonical route template against
  `role_permissions`. Route handlers do not check role names.

## Tenant transaction wiring

Every repository call goes through `TxManager.WithTx`, which opens a
transaction and runs:

```sql
SET LOCAL ROLE erun_tenant;             -- or erun_operations
SELECT set_config('erun.tenant_id', '<uuid>', true);
SELECT set_config('erun.user_id', '<uuid>', true);  -- when relevant
```

RLS policies on tenant-owned tables enforce isolation from there.

## Adding a domain entity

1. Add `internal/model/<entity>.go` — Bun-tagged struct.
2. Add `internal/repository/<entity>.go` — `Create`/`Get`/`List`/`Update`.
3. Add `internal/routes/<entity>.go` — `Register<Entity>Routes`.
4. Wire it in `server.go` `NewHandler` (construct repo, call register).
5. `go build ./...` and `go test ./...`.

Reuse `model` structs as the entity language across layers; do not
introduce DTOs.

## IDs

- All externally visible IDs are UUIDv7 from database defaults
  (`DEFAULT uuidv7()`). Application code does not generate or accept them
  on create.

## Audit logging

Authentication middleware writes API audit events automatically using
the canonical route template. Routes do not hand-write routine audit.

## Validation

```sh
go mod tidy
go build ./...
go test ./...
```

For end-to-end checks, exercise against a local PostgreSQL with the
matching `erun-backend-db`-shaped schema:

- `GET /healthz` → 204
- `GET /v1/whoami` (no token) → 401
- `GET /v1/whoami` (valid token, empty DB) → bootstraps + 200
- `GET /v1/whoami` (valid token, unknown user, non-empty DB) → 401
